---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const pageTitleZh = '词汇的失地：城市化如何让词语失去地方、身体与生态参照物';
const pageTitleEn =
  'Displaced Vocabulary: How Urbanization Detaches Words from Place, Body, and Ecological Referents';
const summaryZh = '城市化并不只改变土地使用，也改变语言与身体之间的距离。';
const summaryEn =
  'Urbanization changes not only land use, but also the distance between language and the body.';
const descriptionZh =
  '城市化并不只改变土地使用，也改变语言与身体之间的距离。本文将自然与农耕词汇视为微型地理档案，讨论词语如何在城市化过程中失去地方、身体与生态参照物。';
const descriptionEn =
  'This essay reads natural and agrarian vocabulary as miniature geographic archives, tracing how words lose place, body, and ecological referents through urbanization.';
const keywordsZh = ['语言地理', '经验消亡', '地方记忆', '无地方性', '文化景观', '城市化'];
const keywordsEn = [
  'linguistic geography',
  'experiential extinction',
  'place memory',
  'placelessness',
  'cultural landscape',
  'urbanization'
];

const openingTextZh =
  '人类语言作为一种动态的社会规约系统，其词汇库的沉淀与演变本质上是特定历史时期人类生存方式的忠实映射。在漫长的农耕文明中，中华民族以高度发达的生态适应和农业实践，锻造出了一个极其丰富且具有深厚“具身性”的语言体系。在这个体系中，大量的成语、词汇以及修辞意境，如“鸟语花香”“如沐春风”等，直接依托于生动的物理世界和感官体验。然而，随着全球规模最大的城市化进程在中国的高速推进，社会空间、劳作方式和生存环境发生了根本性重塑。';
const openingTextEn =
  'Human language is a dynamic system of social convention, and the sedimentation of its vocabulary faithfully records the ways people lived in particular historical periods. Across a long agrarian civilization, ecological adaptation and agricultural practice produced a richly embodied linguistic system. Many idioms, words, and rhetorical images, such as 鸟语花香 (niao yu hua xiang) and 如沐春风 (ru mu chun feng), rely directly on a vivid physical world and sensory experience. Yet as China has undergone the largest and fastest urbanization process in the world, social space, labor, and everyday environments have been fundamentally remade.';
const mechanismIntroZh =
  '词语并不是凭空漂浮的符号。它们依靠身体、地方、物种、天气、劳动和代际记忆来维持意义。当这些现实参照物从日常生活中退场，词语仍然可以继续流通，但其经验厚度会逐渐变薄。';
const mechanismIntroEn =
  'Words are not free-floating signs. They rely on bodies, places, species, weather, labor, and intergenerational memory to sustain meaning. When these real referents withdraw from everyday life, words may still circulate, but their experiential thickness gradually thins.';
const lexiconIntroZh =
  '以下词语并非简单“消失”，而是在城市化语境中发生了不同形式的漂移：有的失去身体经验，有的转为抽象隐喻，有的进入商业命名，有的成为屏幕化的自然想象。';
const lexiconIntroEn =
  'The words below do not simply “disappear.” In urbanized contexts, they drift in different ways: some lose bodily experience, some become abstract metaphors, some enter commercial naming, and some become screen-mediated imaginations of nature.';

const mechanismItems = [
  {
    tag: 'place',
    titleZh: '土地使用变化',
    titleEn: 'Land-Use Change',
    textZh: '农田、荒地、湿地、村落与地方性景观被城市建设、道路系统和标准化空间重新组织。地方并未完全消失，但其生态细节、劳作节奏与物候结构被不断压缩。',
    textEn:
      'Farmland, wasteland, wetlands, villages, and local landscapes are reorganized by urban construction, road systems, and standardized space. Place does not disappear completely, but its ecological details, labor rhythms, and phenological structure are compressed.',
